<title>ITALY: Ansaldo wins 250 bln lire U.K. deal.</title>
<headline>Ansaldo wins 250 bln lire U.K. deal.</headline>
<dateline>GENOA, Italy 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Ansaldo Trasporti SpA said it had won a contract worth a total 250 billion lire from the Greater Manchester Passenger Transport Authority (GMPTA) to build an extension to the Manchester Metrolink system.</p>
<p>Ansaldo, part of the Finmeccanica group, said in a statement the construction will be carried out by project financing, with GMPTA contributing 25 million sterling, the European Development Fund 10 million stg and property owners in the areas concerned putting in six million stg.</p>
<p>The rest will be covered by private capital and by the British government.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
